{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794076382,"nonce":"8Dvx9zEszm4SjSbaXO+7X+7USB8=","title":"Motion demo loses its entrance animation after any theme switch","message":"Reproduced on the live site (blinc.rs/components/layout/motion/, Live tab, headless Chrome). The \"Toggle feed\" button shows and hides a `motion()` feed with a staggered fade-in.\n\nBefore any theme change, every show animates: feed-area brightness ramps 21 to 29 to 33 across frames sampled at 50, 250 and 500 ms, repeated four times. After switching theme (Expressive, Restrained, or back to Hybrid), every show is at full brightness on the first sampled frame, for at least three toggles per theme. The entrance never plays again until the page is reloaded. (One earlier run showed the animation come back on the second toggle after one switch; the later runs did not, so treat recovery as unreliable.)\n\nKey: the motion has a stable key. `motion()` derives it from its call site plus an index, and `.id(\"demo-activity-motion\")` appends a suffix, so it is the same across rebuilds. The key being stable is the likely reason state survives the theme rebuild.\n\nThe worker's `theme()` calls `ThemeState::init` (family change) or `set_scheme`, then `request_rebuild()`.\n\nLead, not confirmed as the cause: the web frame loop in blinc_app never calls `begin_stable_motion_frame()` or `reset_stable_motions_for_rebuild()`, which the windowed rebuild path calls every frame and on every full rebuild. It does call `end_stable_motion_frame()`. That alone does not explain why the first show works, so check the web path with tracing before changing it.\n\nNext step: a headless recorder test that builds the demo, toggles, rebuilds as a theme switch does, and toggles again, asserting the motion state is Entering after the second show.","files":null}]}